@@ -8305,3 +8305,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-02: RISK-COVERAGE ABSTENTION characterization of the proven 0.9131 discriminator — convert proven DISCRIMINATION (not SELECTION, which is closed) into a deployable SELECTIVE-PREDICTION operating envelope: the risk-coverage curve (AURC), risk@coverage operating points, and calibration of the shipped math-only detector as an abstention gate. Does the ENERGY signal beat the entropy/self-certainty baseline as a selective-prediction signal (arXiv:2603.21172 shows entropy fails)? This is the on-mission product framing (abstain when likely-wrong), distinct from the CLOSED best-of-N selection question (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: energy_is_a_better_selective_prediction_signal_than_entropy_deployable_abstention_gate; results/experiment_3718_risk_coverage_abstention_characterization.json
 - 2026-06-02: REPLICATE the headline-class step-error discrimination on a FRESH corpus — measure the verifier ensemble's AUROC on a DIFFERENT step-error corpus (a fresh PRM/ProcessBench-style set, NOT FoVer) to show the 0.9131-class discrimination generalizes beyond FoVer (G1 strengthening, the north-star-sanctioned 'new corpus' move). The frozen 0.9131 stays frozen; this is a SUPPORTING second datapoint, not a re-freeze (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: headline_discrimination_is_fover_specific_generalization_narrowed_honest; results/experiment_3719_headline_replication_fresh_corpus.json
 - 2026-06-02: FR-11 continuous self-learning v14 — distribution-SHIFT robustness of the consolidated template library: apply a v13-consolidated template to a fresh session drawn from a DIFFERENT slice (forward diff from v13's same-distribution transfer) and confirm it either still beats cold-start OR conservatively falls back without collapse — the Tier-2->Tier-4 robustness step (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: fr11_v14_template_falls_back_gracefully_under_shift_no_collapse; results/experiment_3720_fr11_continuous_self_learning_v14.json
+- 2026-06-02: Hardware continuity (consolidated, all 3 boards) — CONFIRM KV260 terminal state (overlay loaded + non-fabricated latency transcript on disk from exp3709) and RECOMMEND the operator lift the per-milestone KV260 mandate (north-star sec-3); PolarFire opportunistic reachability; GateMate documentation-only (openFPGALoader missing). SSH-reachability preconditions only; NO host SD-card check; NO speedup claim (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: kv260_terminal_confirmed_mandate_lift_recommended_polarfire_gatemate_audited; results/experiment_3721_hardware_kv260_terminal_confirm_and_continuity.json
